## Design (non-negotiable)

Priority: fun → easy → clear → selective → respectful. Fun is consequence and rhythm, not decoration.

- Dark, matte, editorial, layered. No neon-terminal chrome. No casino glow.
- Tokens only: `frontend/src/styles/tokens.css`, `frontend/src/styles/product-hierarchy.css`, `frontend/src/styles/product-rhythm.css`, `frontend/src/styles/fantasy-phone.css`.
- Blue (`--experience-blue` / `--accent`) = current context and the next action. Nothing else.
- Teal = healthy/saved. Amber = attention. Red = destructive/blocking. Gold = awards only.
- Hierarchy from surface, type, and spacing — not a border on every box. Every page, mobile and desktop, uses token insets and gutters; text is never flush to a line and never smaller than `--text-xs`.
- Editorial pages use `HubExperienceHero` + `HubExperienceLayout` + `HubExperienceSummary` from `frontend/src/DraftHub/HubUILayout.jsx`.
- Before UI work, resolve `frontend/src/livingSurfaces.js` and match that row’s `page` and `copy`. Do not invent chrome.
- Live draft rooms stay board-first. Do not wrap them in settings chrome.
- On phone: destination title + one overflow. A one-row league strip (name + caret; New league / Sync in the caret; Needs attention one line) sits under the picker so heroes stay above the fold. No stacked brand, context, or tab strips. Weekly and season boards are dense ranking rows. Weekly phone: one sticky bar (position, filter, count); movement chips and search live in the filter sheet. Compare is one toolbar control, never a checkbox on every card. Bottom nav says Projections. Idle Draft and Mock share one seat component so the live room inherits it.
- Copy lives in `*Presentation.js` (or an existing copy module). State the decision and the cost of getting it wrong. No slogan that could sit on another app. No “Submit”, no “You do not have permission” (use “Commissioner managed”).
- Motion 120–200ms. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. No sound except opt-in live-draft audio.

## Product rules you may not bypass

- League policy changes apply to **new contracts only**. Say that once, next to Save. Do not mention a migration unless a control exists.
- Applying a league template confirms, names what changes, and fills the form. It does not save. Offer undo until the next edit. Style those triggers as destructive.
- Players-tab adds follow the acquisition calendar (`acquisitionWindow.js`). Staff Roster management may override; Players-tab adds may not.
- Do not invent a parallel rules or contract model. Merge/validate via `rulesPresentation.js`. Backend is authoritative.
- Same player photos on mock boards, nominee cards, rails, and rosters. Hub media and remote photos request the painted size (`?w=48/96/256`). Do not ship the studio original on every page.
- New work reuses destinations, chrome, and tokens. Do not start a new aesthetic.
- Fantasy lists people by **owner name**. Team nicknames may sit underneath or after a middot. Never show a team nickname as the only identity when an owner is known.
- This-week player notes are Sleeper locker or practice plus an optional projection delta. Do not bake YouTube show copy as current-week narrative.
- Weekly compare is a mode: enter Compare, then row clicks (not the name) select. Never always-on checkboxes.
- Weekly board rows match across positions. Opportunity, role-up, and commentary live in the inspector, not extra table chips.
- Player inspector is hero-first: one P50, floor/ceiling inline, one read strip. Do not restore the 2×2 insight grid.
- One injury mark per weekly row (compact Q / D / P). Never a second status pill under the name.
- Draft availability shows current and future times only. Commissioners lock a promising overlap as draft night, or the tapped hour even when no overlap exists yet. Idle Draft is the calendar plus a compact room strip — do not stack a second date/time card and a Who is in list on the same scroll. Closed calendar + no locked night: off-calendar lock is the primary. Seating pill counts claimed teams and is amber below a full room, teal only at 12/12. Locked night shows in the viewer’s timezone; Draft setup names league time once. Home "Not scheduled" links to Draft. Home names a roster hole over a commissioner invite. This Week hero follows board state — never “No swap worth making” over an error. Gate hero copy on load. Hero states the lineup-call count once. Empty slots say Empty; Waiting on roster is the missing-roster rail. Swap cards are attention amber with a Start action; wide range is a quiet marker, never a card-wide amber border or primary blue. Refresh projections sits on the freshness line. Bench uses the same cards and spans under the rail. Name the Vibes / VA-projections number. Game center unscored state is “No scores yet”, not Waiting. Sync league is the routine strip action; New league is a quieter create control.
- Suggested bid names scoring and Rules risk posture. Never show "Hub" in UI copy.
- Best ball: leftmost # is monotonic; Pos rank groups by position; missing ECR is a No ECR chip/filter, never a dash; Edge names ±10 in copy (teal discount, `--tone-negative` reach, never amber); labeled Pos / ECR / Sort menus; page-owned windowed scroll; Scoring: PPR; no roadmap notes in user copy.
- On Cap, leftover plus against-cap (salary + dead) equals the cap, and every figure names what it counts. After-this-move leftover sits next to the cut and bid.
- Teal only for healthy/saved (full room, synced, saved). Red is destructive only — not a P50 delta. Gold is awards only. Chat launcher stays flush to an edge and expands on hover.
- Seat is the slot; manager is the person. Add a seat only past the seat count. Access & imports is email-assign and the Sleeper link; Draft owns the invite link; the strip owns Sync league.
- Mark draft complete is a Contracts red confirm. Setup shows status only.
- Transactional SMS is opt-in only. Phone lives on the account. SMS is never a league invite. Privacy and Terms must name the vendor, non-sharing of mobile numbers, frequency, and “message and data rates may apply.”
- Trades cap line is **current roster** salary. My team **{season} committed** is draft-surviving salary. Do not use one "committed" for both.
- Auto-check every trade package and gate Propose on a pass. The verdict is a colored live status banner next to the primary.
- Ideas need chips are starter-thin positions only. Extra depth (6 RB) is surplus, not a need.

